At resonance condition, $\mathrm{X}_{\mathrm{C}}=\mathrm{X}_{\mathrm{L}}$ The impedance is given as: $\begin{aligned} \mathrm{Z}=\sqrt{\mathrm{R}^2+\left(\mathrm{X}_{\mathrm{L}}-\mathrm{X}_{\mathrm{C}}\right)^2}\\ \mathrm{Z}=\mathrm{R}=2 \Omega \\ \mathrm{I}_{\mathrm{rms}}=\frac{\mathrm{e}_{\mathrm{mms}}}{\mathrm{R}}\\ \mathrm{I}_{\mathrm{rms}}=\frac{0.1}{2}=0.05 \mathrm{ A}\\ \omega=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\mathrm{LC}}}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{10^{-4} \times 4 \times 10^{-10}}}\\ \omega=5 \times10^6
\end{aligned} $\therefore \quad The $voltage-drop across the inductor is, \begin{aligned} \mathrm{V}=\mathrm{I}_{\mathrm{rms}} \times \mathrm{X}_{\mathrm{L}}=\mathrm{I}_{\mathrm{rms}} \times \mathrm{L} \omega\\ \mathrm{V}=0.05 \times10^{-4} \times5 \times10^6 \\ \mathrm{ V}=25 \mathrm{ V}
\end{aligned}$

